-- Step 143. Fully funded and partial bachelors scholarships found on scholarshipsads.com (US and Australia), read 1 Nov 2026.
-- SOURCE: scholarshipsads.com listing pages. That site re-posts scholarship news and is NOT an official source, so nothing here is confirmed.
-- Each row says NOT YET CHECKED and has verified = false. Where the listing gave the school's own link it is used, otherwise the link is the listing page.
-- Rows with no school in our database (Duke, American University, Richmond, Emory) are added with no school attached, so they still show on the Scholarships page.
-- Left out: Australia Awards (masters only for Ghana), Excelsior (listing could not be opened) and awards for current students only.
-- Safe to run more than once.
drop table if exists pg_temp._new_ads;
create temp table _new_ads as
select * from (values
(null::text, $q$American University$q$, $q$United States$q$, $q$Emerging Global Leader Scholarship$q$, $q$Full$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a listing on scholarshipsads.com, a third-party site that re-posts scholarship news, so the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the university's own page before you rely on it. For international first-year applicants (not US citizens, permanent residents or dual US citizens). Needs strong academic results, leadership and community involvement, interest in civic engagement and social change, and a commitment to improving underserved communities. You must not have started university study in the US or at home. You must meet AU's admission and secondary-school graduation rules. Apply through AU's admissions system with the scholarship instructions. The page does not mention Ghana or Africa, and nothing in the stated criteria excludes Ghana. Deadline 1 November 2026. The listing says graduate aid is separate.$q$, $q$Full tuition, room and board, renewable for up to four years. Not covered: health insurance, books, airfare, personal expenses.$q$, $q$2026-11-01$q$, $q$https://www.american.edu/admissions/international/au-egl-scholarship.cfm$q$),
(null::text, $q$Duke University$q$, $q$United States$q$, $q$Karsh International Scholarship$q$, $q$Full$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a listing on scholarshipsads.com, a third-party site that re-posts scholarship news, so the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the university's own page before you rely on it. For incoming first-year international applicants (not US citizens or permanent residents, and not dual US citizens) with demonstrated financial need. There is no separate application: apply for Duke undergraduate admission, say you want financial aid, then complete the CSS Profile and any financial documents Duke asks for, plus transcripts, recommendation letters and essays. If you do not tick financial aid at admission you may not be able to ask for institutional aid later. No minimum GPA is stated. The listing says applicants from a wide range of countries may be considered and does not name Ghana. Duke aid deadlines on the listing: Early Decision 3 November, Regular Decision 1 February. Confirm the dates for your entry year.$q$, $q$Full tuition, university housing and meals, mandatory fees, extra support for demonstrated need, and funding for three summers of research, unpaid internships and other opportunities.$q$, null::text, $q$https://www.scholarshipsads.com/karsh-duke-university-scholarship$q$),
($q$University of Virginia-Main Campus$q$, $q$Jefferson Scholars Foundation / University of Virginia$q$, $q$United States$q$, $q$Jefferson Scholarship$q$, $q$Full$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a listing on scholarshipsads.com, a third-party site that re-posts scholarship news, so the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the university's own page before you rely on it. For students in their final school year who are nominated by their school (you cannot nominate yourself). International students can be considered because citizenship is not a selection criterion. You must meet UVA's undergraduate admission requirements and apply to UVA separately (Early Decision, Early Action or Regular Decision). Not previously nominated for a Jefferson or Walentas Scholarship. Based on academic strength, leadership and citizenship. Financial need is not considered. Nomination materials: the school sends nominee information, one recommendation letter, a transcript and the school profile. You send contact details, activities, awards, a personal essay and a leadership essay. Regional interviews are usually in January and final interviews in late February. The listing does not name Ghana: your school must take part in the nomination process, so ask the Foundation or UVA. Deadline 1 December 2026 for both the school and student materials. Decisions are generally due in mid-April.$q$, $q$Intended to cover the full cost of attendance for four years: tuition, room and board, enrichment, international travel and career development. The Foundation lists more than USD 42,000 a year for Virginia residents and more than USD 83,000 a year for non-residents.$q$, $q$2026-12-01$q$, $q$https://www.scholarshipsads.com/jefferson-scholarship-fully-funded-scholarship-in-usa$q$),
(null::text, $q$University of Richmond$q$, $q$United States$q$, $q$Richmond Scholars Program$q$, $q$Full$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a listing on scholarshipsads.com, a third-party site that re-posts scholarship news, so the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the university's own page before you rely on it. Open to US and international first-year applicants. No separate application: submit a complete first-year admission application by 1 December 2026 and everyone who applies by then is considered. Meet first-year admission rules: a high school diploma or equivalent and 16 units of secondary coursework. Needs academic achievement, leadership, a strong sense of purpose and interest in a diverse, inclusive community. SAT and ACT are optional for 2027. Non-native English speakers need TOEFL, IELTS or Duolingo or an approved waiver. Competitive scores listed are TOEFL iBT 100, IELTS 7.5, Duolingo 135, which are not minimums. Finalists are told by 1 February, interviews are by Zoom in mid-February, and final selections are by 1 March. The listing does not name Ghana, so confirm with the university.$q$, $q$Full tuition, housing and food for up to eight consecutive semesters, a one-time USD 5,500 enrichment grant, guaranteed on-campus housing, priority registration and faculty mentors. Other personal and educational costs may not be covered.$q$, $q$2026-12-01$q$, $q$https://www.scholarshipsads.com/richmond-scholars-program-fully-funded-undergraduate-scholarship-in-usa$q$),
(null::text, $q$Emory University$q$, $q$United States$q$, $q$Emory Scholar Programs$q$, $q$Partial$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a listing on scholarshipsads.com, a third-party site that re-posts scholarship news, so the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the university's own page before you rely on it. Open to first-year applicants of all nationalities starting Fall 2027, in Emory College of Arts and Sciences, Oxford College, or both. No separate application, nomination or scholarship essay: submit the Common Application and answer Yes when asked about Scholar Programs. Needs a complete Emory admission application with transcripts, school report, recommendations, personal statement, Emory short answers and English-language evidence where required. Based on academic excellence, leadership or initiative, community contribution and intellectual curiosity. No minimum GPA is published. Check Emory's SAT and ACT rule for Fall 2027. The listing does not name Ghana. Deadlines: main 15 November 2026, Early Decision I (binding) 1 November 2026. Finalists are told by the end of February and decisions come around late March.$q$, $q$Partial to full merit scholarship, with potentially substantial tuition support. Renewable for up to eight semesters. Also early registration, faculty mentorship and leadership programming. The listing title says fully funded but the text says merit-based, so the amount is unclear.$q$, $q$2026-11-15$q$, $q$https://www.scholarshipsads.com/emory-university-fully-funded-scholarships-2027-in-usa-25jul2026$q$),
($q$University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill$q$, $q$University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill$q$, $q$United States$q$, $q$Morehead-Cain Scholarship$q$, $q$Full$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a listing on scholarshipsads.com, a third-party site that re-posts scholarship news, so the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the university's own page before you rely on it. The listing says this is a fully funded bachelors scholarship at UNC Chapel Hill. I could not open the listing page, so eligibility for international students and Ghana, requirements, amounts and deadlines are NOT STATED here. Check with UNC before planning around it.$q$, $q$Listed as fully funded. Details not stated.$q$, null::text, $q$https://www.scholarshipsads.com/morehead-cain-scholarship-at-the-university-of-north-carolina-usa-22jul2026$q$),
($q$University of Arizona$q$, $q$Stamps Scholars Foundation$q$, $q$United States$q$, $q$Stamps Scholars Program$q$, $q$Partial$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a listing on scholarshipsads.com, a third-party site that re-posts scholarship news, so the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the university's own page before you rely on it. Stamps Scholars is run by the Stamps Scholars Foundation with partner universities. You cannot apply to the Foundation directly: you apply for undergraduate admission at a partner university and follow that university's Stamps page, which says whether a separate application is needed. Most partners award first-year entrants. Based on academic merit, leadership potential and character. Financial need is not considered. The listing says international students may be eligible at some partner universities but not all, and does not name Ghana, so confirm with this university. Typical materials: transcripts, admission application, personal statement and essays, leadership and activities, recommendation letters, test scores where required, and possibly an interview. There is no single deadline: dates vary by university, from October to January or later. The partner list can change and not every partner is taking applications.$q$, $q$Typically up to the full cost of attendance, but packages differ by university. Per the Foundation as quoted on the listing: annual awards of USD 20,000 to 98,000. May include tuition, room and board, and enrichment funding for study abroad, research, internships and conferences.$q$, null::text, $q$https://www.scholarshipsads.com/stamps-scholars-program-in-usa-fully-funded$q$),
